# Copy to .env and edit. Only read the first time Dzomdu starts; after that, change the
# language model and vault in the app's Settings page.

# Needed once to download the speaker-recognition model.
#  1. Accept the terms at https://huggingface.co/pyannote/speaker-diarization-community-1
#  2. Create a Read token at https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens
HF_TOKEN=

# --- Language model for summaries: choose ONE -------------------------------------------
# A) Ollama on this computer (the default; best on a Mac since Docker can't use its GPU)
#    Install Ollama, run `ollama pull qwen3:14b`, then leave these as they are.
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434
# LLM_MODEL=qwen3:14b

# B) Ollama Cloud: nothing to download. Transcripts are sent to Ollama.
#    Create a key at https://ollama.com/settings/keys
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://ollama.com
# LLM_MODEL=gpt-oss:120b
# LLM_API_KEY=

# C) Ollama in Docker: docker compose --profile local-llm up -d
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://ollama:11434

# --- Speech to text ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# tiny, base, small (default), medium, large-v3-turbo (most accurate, needs more CPU/RAM)
# DZOMDU_ASR_MODEL=small
# DZOMDU_ASR_LANGUAGE=en

# Port on this computer
# DZOMDU_PORT=8765
